# <Project Name> — Design System

## Resume prompt
Paste this into a new Claude Design session (or it will be picked up
automatically via `/design-sync` if this repo is linked to Claude Code):

> Read /design/DESIGN.md and /design/design-system-spec.json before
> generating anything. Match existing tokens and components exactly; flag
> anything that doesn't map to an existing pattern instead of inventing a
> new one.

---

## 1. Visual theme & atmosphere
<!-- What kind of product this looks like, in a sentence or two. -->

## 2. Color
<!-- Semantic roles: primary, secondary, background, surface, text, border,
     success/warning/error. List hex/hsl values grouped by role. -->

## 3. Typography
<!-- Font family, scale (sizes used), weights. -->

## 4. Spacing scale
<!-- The base unit and the scale built from it (e.g. 4px base: 4/8/12/16/24/32). -->

## 5. Component inventory
<!-- Every component Claude Design generated: Button, Card, Input, Nav,
     Modal, etc. One line each: name, variants, where it's used. -->

## 6. Layout patterns
<!-- Grid/columns, breakpoints, common page shapes. -->

## 7. Interaction & motion
<!-- Hover/focus states, transitions, anything animated. -->

## 8. UX decisions & rationale
<!-- Why a pattern was chosen over the alternative — this is what a flat
     screenshot loses. Keep it to decisions that would otherwise get
     re-litigated later. -->

## 9. Known gaps / TBD
<!-- Anything not yet decided — empty/loading/error states, mobile
     behavior, edge cases. Mark explicitly rather than leaving silent. -->
